# What Prettier must not touch, and why.
#
# CLAUDE.md §3.1 says "ESLint and Prettier enforced pre-commit and in CI".
# That was true of ESLint and never of Prettier: `verify` ran typecheck, lint
# and the unit projects, and the Husky hook runs `verify`, so nothing ever
# checked formatting. 407 files had drifted by the time it was noticed. This
# file plus the `format:check` step in `verify` make the agreement true.

# THE HANDOFF IS EVIDENCE, NOT SOURCE. Every phase diffs its implementation
# against these files value by value, and three of them (SCREENS.md,
# DATA_MODEL.md, SECURITY.md) are quoted verbatim in tests and deviations.
# Reformatting them would rewrite the thing every spec-compliance pass is
# measured against, and a later reader could not tell our wrapping from the
# designer's. Nothing in here is ours to touch.
handoff/

# Scratch and generated artefacts: the SDD workspace (plans' ledgers, briefs,
# reports, review packages) and every build output. Formatting untracked output
# is churn nobody reads.
#
# This block said "Git-ignored scratch" from Phase 0 until Phase 3 Task 8, and
# `.superpowers/` was not in `.gitignore` at all — the comment described a
# state that had never existed. It is ignored now; the claim and the fact were
# made to agree in the same commit rather than the sentence being quietly
# softened.
.superpowers/
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
.lighthouseci/
lhci-reports/
.next/
dist/
build/
node_modules/

# Agent git worktrees: a second checkout of THIS repository, one directory
# deep under `.claude/`, whose files are formatted and checked in their own
# checkout on their own branch. Formatting a duplicate here would either churn
# another session's working tree or fail this gate on a file that is not ours
# to touch — `prettier --check .` flags the nested copy of
# `apps/web/payload-types.ts`, because the entry for that path below carries a
# slash and is therefore anchored to the repository root.
#
# `.claude/` itself is NOT ignored: `.claude/skills/` holds the two browser-QA
# skills CLAUDE.md §10 makes mandatory, and they are tracked source.
#
# The trailing slash matters beyond Prettier: `adminGuardRegistration.test.ts`
# turns every directory line in this file into a probe and requires ESLint to
# ignore it too, so this line and `eslint.config.js`'s `.claude/worktrees/**`
# are pinned to each other by a test rather than by a convention.
.claude/worktrees/

# The agent harness rewrites this while a session runs, so checking it makes
# the gate's outcome depend on what the harness did since the last clean.
# Listed here as well as in `.gitignore` because this file is where "what
# Prettier must not touch" is stated, rather than relying on Prettier 3's
# default of also reading `.gitignore`. It is a FILE, not a directory, so it
# adds no probe to `adminGuardRegistration.test.ts`'s ESLint parity case — and
# it needs none: nothing in `eslint.config.js` lints `.json`.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Generated by Payload from the collections; regenerating it would undo any
# formatting we applied, so checking it would fail on the next `payload
# generate:types`.
apps/web/payload-types.ts

# Binary and lockfiles Prettier would either mangle or churn.
*.png
*.woff2
package-lock.json
